| 1 | 3 | Parts of wellness. *What does each part of my health need, and who else does a habit help?* | 4 | g3-phw-wellness-actions; g3-phw-habits-look-closely; g3-pa-active-and-invite | NHES.S1.5.2; NHES.S7.5.1 | Practicing healthy behaviors (standard 7): looking closely at a habit (what it is, when, who it helps) | Day 1: wellness has parts (physical, mental and emotional, social); each student builds a wellness wheel with one real action per part and says why it helps (NHES.S1.5.2); retrieval of g2-phw-why-health-matters (grade 2 unit 12). Day 2: habits looked at closely: enough sleep, sunscreen and shade, safe sound volume, washing; for each, who benefits (me, my class), so habits help self and others (NHES.S7.5.1); retrieval of g2-phw-stopping-germs. Day 3: an hour of activity a day and the three kinds that build the heart, muscles and flexibility; warm up, cool down, drink water; notice someone left out and invite them, with an invite line (~NHES.S8.5.1 and ~NHES.S1.5.2 practice; health teaches the why and the plan, PE the moving); retrieval of g2-pa-invite-friends-to-move (grade 2 unit 15). Day 4: end-of-unit check: unseen short scenarios: an action for each part of wellness for a character, who benefits from a habit and why, an invite line for a left-out character; valuing item on a character who skips sleep. Out: body systems (science grade 4), fitness scores. Serves HECAT.PHW.HBO1, HBO2, HBO3, HBO4, HBO7; PA.HBO1, HBO2, HBO3, HBO4, HBO7. Tools: wellness wheel sheet. Curio Class writes: the wheel, habit cards, invite line card. Cost (class of 30, provisional): $3 printing | First because the parts of wellness are what every later unit sorts by, and the habits retrieve grade 2 unit 12 at once. Activity sits here, in weeks 1 to 4, so PE grade 3's active-outside row has health's why behind it (Cross-subject) | Candidate: HECAT PHW module 3-5 read may add dental care (brushing and flossing); one line inside day 2 | Never ask about a child's bedtime, home screen