| 2 | 3 | What shapes my health. *What pushes a person toward or away from a healthy habit, and how do I spot it?* | 5 | g3-phw-influences-on-health; g3-fn-food-groups; g3-fn-added-sugar-drinks; g3-t-tobacco-facts | NHES.S2.5.1 | Analyzing influences (standard 2): the influence check, grade 3 form (name it, say how it pushes) | Day 1: things that shape health: family, friends, media, school and the place we live; the influence check modeled on a character's case (NHES.S2.5.1); retrieval of g2-meh-people-are-different (grade 2 unit 14). Day 2: the food groups and what each does for a growing body, a range of foods from each (including fortified dairy swaps), foods for every day and foods for sometimes (~NHES.S1.5.2 practice); retrieval of g2-fn-pick-best-snack (grade 2 unit 12). Day 3: added sugar and where it hides; reading the sugar line on two invented drink labels and comparing the two whole numbers; water and milk as everyday drinks; pairs run the influence check on a drink ad (~NHES.S1.5.2, ~NHES.S2.5.1 practice). Day 4: what nicotine is, what smoke and vapor do to lungs and to people nearby, and the norm said plainly, "most people your age do not smoke or vape" (CDC youth tobacco pages, nearest age group, source and year at the expert read); the influence check on an invented vape ad without the card (~NHES.S2.5.1 application); retrieval of g2-t-no-thanks-smoke (grade 2 unit 13). Day 5: end-of-unit check: unseen short cases: run the influence check on a new ad or a friend's push; name a food group's job; pick the everyday drink from two labels and give the reason. Out: calories, daily sugar amounts in grams, any weight talk. Serves HECAT.PHW.HBO1, HBO6; FN.HBO1 to HBO8; T.HBO1, HBO2, HBO3, HBO4. Facts and sources: added sugar and the label (the federal food and drug agency's label pages), food groups (USDA's food guide pages), nicotine (CDC). Tools: influence check card, label cards. Curio Class writes: two invented drink labels, an invented drink ad and an invented vape ad with no product names, food group cards. Cost: $3 printing; clean empty drink containers the teacher brings, optional | After unit 1 because influences push on the habits unit 1 named. Food, drinks and tobacco share one skill (the influence check) across three topics, so the card is modeled, held in pairs and withdrawn inside one unit. Before unit 3, whose careful choices meet the same pushes | Candidate: HECAT FN and T module 3-5 reads may add breakfast and "secondhand smoke at home is not the child's fault"; one line each inside days 2 and 4 | Food: never ask what a child eats or drinks at home; foods and budgets vary; no good or bad foods, no calories, no weighing; no tasting. A child who lives with someone who smokes or vapes is never made to feel blame for that person. No scare images of lungs. Agent reads: sensitivity (food sources named in the brief); safety (containers) |
| 3 | 3 | Helpers and careful choices. *Which helper fits which problem, and when do I stop and think before I choose?* | 5 | g3-s-which-helper; g3-phw-find-resources; g3-s-decide-careful; g3-s-stay-safe-places; g3-aod-medicine-rules | NHES.S3.5.1; NHES.S3.5.2; NHES.S5.5.1 | Accessing help (standard 3): help-steps, the second step (pick the right helper and the right words); deciding (standard 5): decision-steps, notice a careful choice | Day 1: which adult or resource fits which situation (a scraped knee, a worry, a lost item, a question about food), picked and said in the help-step words (NHES.S3.5.1); retrieval of g2-s-find-school-helpers (grade 2 unit 13). Day 2: wellness resources at home, at school and in the community (nurse, clinic, library, a trusted website a teacher names), and each student builds a one-page "where to go" list with a family or school adult (NHES.S3.5.2); medicines only as directed by a trusted adult and first plain facts on alcohol: it is not for children and why (~NHES.S3.5.1 practice); retrieval of g2-phw-doctor-nurse-visit. Day 3: situations that call for careful thinking before choosing (a dare, a medicine, a stranger online, a risky play spot), sorted from easy choices (NHES.S5.5.1). Day 4: safety at home, in a car, near water, on a bike and online in its simplest form (ask before you click, no private details): students decide for a set of cases with the reason, without the card (~NHES.S5.5.1 application); emergency rule kept from grade 2: get an adult first; if no adult can help, call 911; retrieval of g2-s-outdoor-and-home-safety. Day 5: end-of-unit check: unseen cases, pick the right helper and the words; spot the careful choice; give the rule and reason for a place. Out: refusal steps (grade 4), alcohol effects beyond "not for children". Serves HECAT.S.HBO1, HBO3, HBO4, HBO5, HBO6, HBO7; PHW.HBO5; AOD.HBO1, HBO2, HBO3. Curio Class writes: helper situation cards, "where to go" sheet, careful-or-easy sort, place cases, a printed invented screen. Cost: $3 printing | The getting-help unit of grade 3 in a non-sensitive place, so units 6 and 7 can be left out, and before the mid-year check so it is sampled. After unit 2 because careful choices meet the pushes unit 2 named. SEL grade 3's ask-for-help row leans on it (Cross-subject) | Candidate: HECAT S module 3-5 read may add fire escape plans and pedestrian safety; one case each inside day 4 | Medicine and alcohol: pictures and invented labels only; never test knowledge of home medicines; a child who lives with someone who drinks is never made to feel blame. The "where to go" list stays with the student. No real number dialed. Agent reads: sensitivity (safety sources named in the brief) |
| 4 | 3 | Saying it, hearing it, and standing up. *How do I say what I need, really listen, and help when someone is bullied?* | 5 | g3-meh-feelings-say; g3-meh-listening; g3-v-bullying; g3-v-my-limits-and-yours | NHES.S4.5.1; NHES.S4.5.2 | Communicating (standard 4): the grade 3 I-statement and the listening steps; boundary steps and conflict steps returned | Day 1: say clearly what I think and need, in a way that helps health: "I feel ___ when ___ because ___. Please ___.", modeled by the teacher on scripts about a friend, a group and a teacher (NHES.S4.5.1); retrieval of g2-meh-feelings-calm-and-talk (grade 2 unit 14). Day 2: careful listening in several places (class, a game, at home, on a call): look, wait, ask one question, say back what you heard; students rate their listening on a card (NHES.S4.5.2). Day 3: bullying is repeated unkind acts that hurt; the roles (the one bullied, the one bullying, bystanders who can help); an upstander line and telling an adult, with a card playing the unkind line (~NHES.S4.5.2 practice: listening to the one hurt); retrieval of g2-v-settle-it-with-words. Day 4: stating a limit (space, belongings, tickling, shared photos) and respecting others' limits with the boundary steps (~NHES.S4.5.4 practice, owned in grade 4 unit 12); retrieval of g2-v-my-limits-say-stop; the I-statement heard from a third of the class. Day 5: end-of-unit check: unseen scripts, write or say the I-statement for a character, the listening steps for a scene, an upstander line; the I-statement heard from the rest of the class. Out: conflict resolution in full (grade 5), online bullying (grade 6). Serves HECAT.MEH.HBO1, HBO2, HBO7, HBO8; V.HBO1, HBO3. Curio Class writes: scripts, step cards, bullying scenes with characters varied in family, ability and culture. Cost: $3 printing | After the mid-year check, when the class knows the routine; the communication unit of grade 3, before unit 6, which uses the boundary steps. SEL grade 3 unit 5 rehearses the upstander plan and SEL unit 1 uses the same feelings words (Cross-subject) | Candidate: HECAT MEH and V module 3-5 reads may add "ways to show care when a friend is upset"; it fits inside day 2 | No child is asked about being bullied or about feelings at home; scenes are characters'. A child being bullied now is never named in a scene; the teacher follows the school's bullying policy if a student tells. No role play of bullying. Agent reads: sensitivity |
| 5 | 3 | Strengths and a goal. *What strength can I grow, and is my goal best done alone or together?* | 3 | g3-phw-grow-strengths; g3-phw-set-goal; g3-phw-goal-alone-or-together | NHES.S1.5.1; NHES.S6.5.1; NHES.S6.5.2 | Setting goals (standard 6): goal-plan returned (say the goal and why) | Day 1: how to grow a strength I already have that keeps me healthy (a calm routine, a sport skill, asking for help) by practicing it and finding a helper (NHES.S1.5.1); one health goal in a sentence from the safe list (sleep, water, handwashing, time outside, screen breaks, a kind act, asking for help) and how it helps health (NHES.S6.5.1); retrieval of g2-phw-why-health-matters and g2-phw-goal-do-it (grade 2 units 12 and 15). Day 2: whether a goal is best done alone, with a helper or as a team (walking to school with friends, a family sleep routine), sorted with a reason (NHES.S6.5.2), with the help-steps' helper step. Day 3: end-of-unit check: the student's own goal sentence with its reason and its alone-or-together choice, or a character's, scored on the goal-plan steps; one unseen sort item. Out: a full plan with resources and a check (grade 4). Serves HECAT.PHW.HBO1, HBO2, HBO7. Curio Class writes: strength cards, goal frame sheet, alone-or-together sort. Cost: $2 printing | Last non-sensitive unit of grade 3, so the goal sentence hands on to grade 4 unit 8 as the first plan, and it closes the year after the communication unit. SEL grade 3 unit 6 sets a school goal on its own card; health's goals stay on the safe health list (Cross-subject) | Candidate: HECAT PHW module 3-5 read may add "name a person who can help with a goal"; inside day 2 | Goals from the safe list only, never weight, body or food limits; a character's goal is always an option; the goal stays with the student. Strengths are never body traits. Agent reads: sensitivity |
