## Cross-subject

### Physical education, grades 3 to 5 (same year)

The physical activity topic is shared (STANDARD.md section 8): health teaches why and the plan, PE teaches the
moving, and the units in each name the other. The PE grades 3 to 5 frame is not written, so this table records the
need from data/progressions/physical-education.csv and gives no PE unit numbers; health weeks are school weeks.

| Health row | Unit here | PE row it names | Needed by | If PE teaches it later |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| g3-pa-active-and-invite | 1 (grade 3 weeks 1 to 4) | g3-active-outside (its row asks health to name it); g3-health-fitness and g3-benefits (the fitness parts and benefits) | Week 3 | Health names the hour a day and the three kinds in one line each and does not teach the fitness parts chart; PE teaches the parts and the trying-it week, and names health's invite line |
| g4-pa-warm-up | 8 (grade 4 weeks 1 to 4) | g4-skill-fitness (warm-up and fitness parts in movement) | Week 3 | Health gives the reason for warm-up, cool-down, water and stopping when hurt and plans the activity week; PE practices them moving |
| g5-pa-habit-practice | 15 (grade 5 weeks 1 to 4) | g5-food-drink (its row asks health to name it); g5-fitt | Week 2 | Health names water before and after activity in the log and in unit 19's snack-day plan and does not teach energy foods for activity; PE teaches food and drink for activity and the FITT plan |

### Social and emotional learning, grades 3 to 5 (same year)

The SEL 3 to 5 rows lean on health rows (data/progressions/sel.csv cross_subject); each SEL row names its own SEL
unit, and the SEL frame sets its weeks, so no SEL week is given here. The two courses use one feelings chart (SEL's),
one calm-down card (SEL's calm-down steps), one I-statement (health's words, grade 3 form "I feel ___ when ___ because
___. Please ___.") and one upstander plan (SEL's), so a skill is not taught twice in a year.

| SEL row | Leans on | Unit here | Note, with the if-later line |
|---|---|---|---|
| g3-sa-name-feelings (SEL unit 1) | g3-meh-feelings-say | 4 (grade 3 weeks 17 to 21) | SEL's unit 1 likely comes first and teaches the feelings words; health uses them. If SEL comes later, health's day 1 names the feeling with SEL's chart words itself |
| g3-rel-ask-offer-help (SEL unit 4) | g3-s-which-helper | 3 (grade 3 weeks 10 to 14) | Health teaches which helper fits a safety problem; SEL's problem size meter uses the same helpers. If SEL comes first, health retrieves the meter's "big problem: a trusted adult" |
| g3-rel-stand-up (SEL unit 5) | g3-v-bullying | 4 | Health teaches what bullying is; SEL rehearses the upstander plan. If SEL comes later, health's day teaches one upstander line and telling an adult itself |
