docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:29:## Findings, most serious first
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:31:### 1. Five nonexistent HECAT outcome numbers sit in the `STANDARD.md` coverage map, plus four map-to-progression mismatches
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:34:- **What is wrong:** CDC's HECAT 2021 Appendix 3 has exactly 81 Healthy Behavior Outcomes: AOD 8, FN 12, MEH 9, PHW 12, PA 7, S 8, SH 10, T 5, V 10 (confirmed in `hecat-topics.txt` and on CDC's HECAT 2021 pages). Five rows of the coverage map in `STANDARD.md` section 4 cite HBO numbers one past the real maximum:
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:42:  - **PHW 12 in 3 to 5:** The 3 to 5 cell (line 74) lists `1 to 11` and Key line 87 says `PHW 12 (fads) is judged in grade 7`, yet `health.csv` line 102 (`g5-fn-claims-that-hurt`) still tags `Serves HECAT.PHW.HBO12`.
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:43:  - **MEH 3 in 3 to 5:** The 3 to 5 cell (line 76) lists `1 to 5, 7 to 9` (including MEH 3, handling conflict), yet no grade 3 to 5 row in `health.csv` serves `HECAT.MEH.HBO3` (`g5-v-conflict-steps`, line 103, cites only `HECAT.V.HBO1, HECAT.V.HBO2`).
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:44:  - **FN 12 in 9 to 12:** The 9 to 12 cell (line 75) lists `10 to 13` (including FN 12), yet no grade 9 row in `health.csv` serves `HECAT.FN.HBO12`.
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:51:| Mental and emotional health (MEH) | 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7 | 1 to 5, 7 to 9 | All; 6 in a sensitive unit (s) | All; 6 in a sensitive unit (s) |
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:58:  In Key line 86, replace `Care-seeking (PHW 10 and 11) starts in K to 2` with `Checkup care-seeking (PHW 11) starts in K to 2 because NHES.S1.2.7 does; treatment care-seeking (PHW 10) starts in 3 to 5.` In `data/progressions/health.csv`, remove `HECAT.PHW.HBO12` from `g5-fn-claims-that-hurt` (line 102) and add `HECAT.MEH.HBO3` to `g5-v-conflict-steps` (line 103); confirm FN 12 placement with Cory (Question 3).
