docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:131:### 4. Sensitive ground: `sensitivity-read.md` is never named in `STANDARD.md` or `APPROACH.md`, and 17 of 22 sensitive rows in `health.csv` omit required safeguards
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:138:     - All nine sexual health rows (`g1-sh-families-and-respect` line 40, `g2-sh-bodies-grow-respect` line 57, `g3-sh-respect-all-people` line 78, `g4-sh-body-changes` line 97, `g5-sh-consent-and-health` line 117, `g6-sh-puberty-and-health` line 138, `g7-sh-relationships-consent` line 158, `g8-sh-prevention-and-health` line 180, `g9-sh-health-and-consent` line 206) omit the family note and disclosure reporting route, and 6 of them omit the leave-out note and what the course still meets without it.
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:139:     - Five violence/body-safety rows (`g2-v-body-safety` line 56, `g5-v-body-safety` line 116, `g7-v-dating-and-sexual-harassment` line 157, `g8-v-dating-and-assault` line 178, `g9-v-abuse-and-dating-violence` line 207) omit the full duty-to-report/no-secrecy reporting route and/or what the course still meets without them.
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:151:### 5. Three owner rows in `data/progressions/health.csv` meet their NHES indicator only in part
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:165:### 6. Course list in `data/courses.csv` does not match the four-course band shape in `STANDARD.md` and `ADOPTION-BAR-SUBJECTS.md`
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:182:### 7. No shorter path is stated for K to 8 or 9 to 12, and default session counts say "about"
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:190:### 8. `STANDARD.md` section 8 cross-subject leans are unkeyed and overstate the life science leans compared with `health.csv`
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:193:- **What is wrong:** `STANDARD.md` section 8 names no specific core skill IDs (so a pre-work reader cannot verify leans from `STANDARD.md` alone) and claims `"body systems, puberty, germs and disease, nutrition chemistry lean on the life science progression; a health unit does not reteach the science model, it uses it."` In `data/progressions/health.csv`, however, only two rows lean on science (`g6-phw-habits-for-each-part` on `science:MS-LS1-1` and `g7-phw-living-with-conditions` on `science:MS-LS1-3`), and three health rows explicitly state body organs, germs, and vaccines as health's own plain facts because NGSS does not cover germs/vaccines and reaches body organs only in grade 4 (`k-phw-body-names` line 3, `g1-phw-stop-germs` line 22, `g4-phw-prevent-illness-injury` line 79). All 15 `cross_subject` entries in `health.csv` (12 distinct codes across ELA, Math, and Science) are real codes taught at or before the leaning grade; note only that `MS-LS1-1` sits in science unit 6.6 (late grade 6) and `6.SP.B.5` sits in late grade 6 math, so the grade 6 health frame must sequence `g6-phw-habits-for-each-part` and `g6-pa-habits-supports-barriers` after those units or supply a just-in-time note.
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:194:- **Cost:** A writer reading `STANDARD.md` section 8 will assume science teaches germs, puberty, and nutrition chemistry and leave those facts out of health lessons.
docs/reviews/prework-health-gemini-2026-11-20.md:198:- **Science:** body systems lean on the life science progression (`MS-LS1-1` in grade 6, `MS-LS1-3` in grade 7); a health unit uses those models rather than reteaching them. Because NGSS does not cover germs, vaccines, or puberty, health states those plain facts directly with dated public health sources.
