200 | 12 | 4 | Thinking it through. *How do I make a choice that is fair to the people it touches?* | 12 | g4-rds-ask-questions; g4-rds-check-facts; g4-rds-good-for-us; g4-rds-solve-problems; g4-rds-think-ahead; g4-rds-who-is-affected; g4-sa-skills-grow; g4-sa-what-interests-me |  | None (SEL). Core link (bar item 9): ela:e4-reasons-evidence, the reasons and evidence a speaker gives for a point | Three groups, with a twelfth session as a second Application for group 2 (the moved session, Days). A two-week practice record starts on session 1 (the carry-out cue). Group 1, questions and claims: a partner interviewed with open questions about a choice the class faces, and how the answers changed the student's idea (RD1); a classmate's claim ("this snack gives you energy") checked against facts from a second source, and the choice made on what the facts show (RD2); a choice's results predicted for oneself and a second person, then compared with what happened in the story (RD4). Group 2, solve and map: a school problem solved by gathering two groups' views (younger students, lunch staff) before choosing and testing a solution, the second Application session given to the gathering (RD3); who a school choice touches mapped, how each group would see it, and the rule or group it answers to (RD7); a choice where one's own well-being and a friend's pull apart (stay up for the friend's call, or sleep before the game), picked with a reason (RD6). Group 3, interests and growth: a purpose added to the private interest log that connects to other people, and who might share the interest (SA9); the student's practice record compared with a story character's, and how another person's feedback changed the practice, never belief alone (SA8). Retrieval: the grade 3 rows (units 2, 5 and 6) in the openings; health grade 4 units 9 and 11 (deciding with help, the source check) open RD6 and RD2 as retrieval where the school runs health. End-of-unit evidence: an unseen scene page (a claim check