202 | 14 | 5 | What drives me. *What keeps me going toward a goal when it costs me something?* | 10 | g5-sa-i-can-try; g5-sa-skills-grow; g5-sa-what-interests-me; g5-sm-plan-and-tidy; g5-sm-set-goal; g5-sm-stay-on-task | CASEL.Self-Awareness.7; CASEL.Self-Awareness.8; CASEL.Self-Awareness.9; CASEL.Self-Management.3; CASEL.Self-Management.4; CASEL.Self-Management.5 | None (SEL). Core link (bar item 9): ela:e5-research, a research project worked over several weeks | Two groups. The four-week goal and the three-week practice record start on session 1 (the carry-out cues) and are judged before the Check session. Group 1, goals and plans: a four-week goal on the goal steps card, tracked weekly, with what to drop decided when two goals compete for time (SM4); a multi-week class project planned backward from a deadline and recovered when a step slips, with what the slip cost (SM5); keeping on task through the long project when friends offer something more fun and when the next step gets hard, using the focus plan and its try-again step (try another way, then ask), and what giving in would cost (SM3; it also teaches AASL.V.D.1, trying again when a task gets hard, placed in SEL by library). Group 2, purpose and setbacks: a stretch goal for a character facing a setback that costs something (a free afternoon), with two steps, a helper and a backup plan (SA7); when a friend in a story says "you're just not good at it", the practice record used to explain the setback as a sign to change strategy or get help, never belief alone (SA8; it also teaches AASL.V.D.2, skill grows with practice and help, placed in SEL by library); a purpose found for an interest that costs practice time, decided privately (SA9). Retrieval: the grade 4 rows (units 8 and 12) in the openings; health grade 5 unit 15's four-week log (weeks 1 to 4) opens SM4 as retrieval where the school runs health. End-of-unit evidence: an unseen page (a backup plan for a character's setback; a setback explained from an invented record; which goal to drop and why) and the focus plan's try-again step rehearsed from an unseen card. The course never records a student's own answer to SA7 or SA9. Carry it out: the weekly goal check. Family activity: plan one family job backward from its deadline. Tools: the goal steps card, the backward planner, the practice record, the focus plan card, the private log. Curio Class writes the planner, the records and cases and the page. Provisional cost for 30: about $10 printing. | After unit 13 because steady feelings come before long goals; its five weeks hold the four-week goal (the progression's pace note). Six sub-skills in two groups of three, each with two Fluency sessions, so 10 sessions. Health grade 5 unit 15 (weeks 1 to 4) starts its goal log first; ELA grade 5 unit 2 (course days 42 to 80) runs its research beside it (Cross-subject). Sessions 11 to 20 of the year, weeks 6 to 10. | Candidate: the class project's backward plan sized so its slip and recovery fall inside the unit | Growth is practice, strategy and help, never belief alone. SA7 plans are a character's; SA9 decisions stay private. Agent reads: sensitivity. |
204 | 16 | 5 | Friends through change. *How do friends stay friends when things change, and when is it time to step back?* | 11 | g5-rel-ask-offer-help; g5-rel-friendships; g5-rel-say-no; g5-rel-settle-disagreements; g5-rel-talk-listen; g5-soc-care-when-struggle; g5-soc-read-feelings; g5-soc-their-view | CASEL.Relationship Skills.1; CASEL.Relationship Skills.2; CASEL.Relationship Skills.5; CASEL.Relationship Skills.6; CASEL.Relationship Skills.8; CASEL.Social Awareness.1; CASEL.Social Awareness.3; CASEL.Social Awareness.4 | None (SEL). Core link (bar item 9): ela:e5-discussion, the same class talk norms and words | Three groups. Group 1, a friend's side: an invented friend whose family is moving across town mid-year, the friend's view taken with the shoes switch and how one's own view would change in that place (SO1); mixed clues from an invented friend who says they are fine but is pulling away, a check-in, the answer respected, and a trusted adult named to tell if the worry stays (SO4); the care steps acted with a partner for an invented friend whose best friend has moved away, even when it costs time with others, and a follow-up planned (SO3). Group 2, talking it through: the full talk turn card in an invented hard conversation about a friendship changing (a friend joins a new group), where saying back costs patience (RS1); a disagreement where any fair solution costs each side something, worked with a partner using the I-statement, and a compromise both can keep (RS5); two invented cases, a friend who will be in a different class next year and a friend who will only play if the student leaves another child out, planned with the I-statement, keeping the first friendship and stepping back from the second with a trusted adult's help, the opening of each talk rehearsed with a partner (RS2). Group 3, help and hold: two problems sized on the meter, then asking a teacher for help when friends are watching rehearsed with a partner playing the teacher, and help offered to an invented new classmate (RS8); the refusal steps against a card character who adds a social cost ("then you're not in our group"), the no held and another friend named to turn to (RS6). Retrieval: the grade 4 rows (units 7, 10 and 11) in the openings; health grade 5 unit 17's refusal steps (weeks 10 to 14) open RS6 as retrieval where the school runs health. End-of-unit evidence: an unseen scene page (mixed clues and a check-in; a compromise where both give something; a friendship to step back from and who helps) and the refusal steps rehearsed with the card playing the social cost. Carry it out: "say back first" in hard class talks. Family activity: plan how to keep in touch with someone far away, real or made up. Tools: the shoes switch card, the talk turn card, the I-statement frame, the problem size meter, the refusal card, scene cards. Curio Class writes the cases and page. Provisional cost for 30: about $10 printing. | After unit 15 because holding a no against a social cost follows checking against a crowd. Eight sub-skills, three groups and 11 sessions. Health grade 5 unit 18 (conflict steps and care, weeks 17 to 19) runs in the same weeks, and unit 17 (refusal, weeks 10 to 14) came before (Cross-subject). Sessions 31 to 41 of the year, weeks 16 to 21. | Candidate: the step-back case worded so it is about leaving someone out, with relationship health left to health | No real friends are named. The teacher or a card plays the pressure and any upset part. Moving and a friend moving away can touch a student's own loss: no student is asked about their own move. Relationship health topics are health's. If a student tells of harm or risk, health's steps. Agent reads: sensitivity (no own move or loss asked). |
