LEARNING: Three groups. Group 1, leading the team: a team task led with the three leading steps, then followed, and how leader and follower saw the same decision (RS7); the class elects a team to carry out a class improvement, each student weighing a classmate's different proposal before voting (SM7); an invented teammate who needs help, help offered without taking over, and a team problem sized on the meter to know when to bring in a trusted adult, both rehearsed with a partner (RS8). Group 2, repair and settle: two friends who land in different groups, the friend's side heard first, then own it, sorry with the I-statement and a plan, rehearsed with a partner (RS2); a team disagreement where both sides have good reasons, each saying the other's view first, then I-statements and a solution that meets both (RS5). Group 3, hold the no and speak up: the refusal steps when a card character urges the whole group to skip the hard part or blame another team, the no held while the friendship is kept (RS6); how a leader and how a follower could each speak up when a teammate is left out, chosen from the upstander options for each role and rehearsed with the I-statement while the teacher or a card plays the unkind act (RS9). Retrieval: the grade 3 rows (units 4 and 5) in the openings; health grade 4 unit 10's help-steps open RS8 as retrieval where the school runs health. End-of-unit evidence: the year-end course-level check after this unit is this unit's end-of-unit assessment (Course-level checks): an unseen scene page (the other side's view said first; a leader's and a follower's speak-up) and the refusal steps rehearsed with the card playing the group's push. Carry it out: "both views first" when a team splits. Family activity: practice a no that keeps the friendship on a pretend case, the adult playing the pusher. Tools: the talk turn card, the I-statement frame, the problem size meter, the refusal card, the upstander plan card. Curio Class writes the team cases and page. Provisional cost for 30: about $10 printing. Begun here, owned in grade 5 (the band's owner year; the grade 5 unit that owns each is in the Seams table): CASEL.Relationship Skills.2, CASEL.Relationship Skills.5, CASEL.Relationship Skills.6, CASEL.Relationship Skills.7, CASEL.Relationship Skills.8, CASEL.Relationship Skills.9, CASEL.Self-Management.7.
WHY: After unit 10 because repair and speaking up start from reading how feelings land. Seven sub-skills, mostly rehearsed by doing, so three groups and 11 sessions, its Check and Respond being the year-end check. Health grade 4 unit 12 (weeks 20 to 24) teaches refusal and speak-up on health topics in the same weeks (Cross-subject; For the lead 4). Sessions 42 to 50 of the year, weeks 21 to 25; the year-end check is sessions 51 and 52.
