LEARNING: Two groups. Group 1, naming the change: mixed feelings about a coming change named and rated for a story character (moving to middle school), two feelings that pull opposite ways, and why naming both helps (SA3); a think-feel-do chain for a character whose friends say middle school is scary, and a balanced thought that keeps to the facts (SA5). Group 2, steady through change: an invented schedule change on a test day, two responses listed and one picked, then the calm-down steps and the chosen response rehearsed in a short scene with a partner, and what reacting would have cost (SM1); a calm-down plan for a time of change, two tools tested in a timed practice (two minutes each on a sand timer), and the one that worked kept with a reason (SM2); what a new situation will ask (a middle school visit, a new team), the chances it offers and what missing them would cost (SO7). Grade 5 is the owner year: each row adds the pressure of change. Retrieval: the grade 4 rows (units 7 and 10) in the openings; health grade 5 unit 15's habit list (the same weeks) names the calm tools, which this unit teaches. End-of-unit evidence: an unseen scene page (two opposite feelings and their clues; a balanced thought; a new situation's chance and its cost) and the calm-down steps with a chosen response rehearsed from an unseen card. Carry it out: "stop, breathe, name it, choose" before a schedule change. Family activity: test two calm tools at home and keep the one that worked. Tools: the feelings faces chart, the chain sheet, the calm-down plan card, sand timers. Curio Class writes the cases, the middle-school-visit scene and the page. Provisional cost for 30: about $9 printing and $6 once for six sand timers where the room has none.
WHY: First because the year's angle, ready for change, starts from feelings and calm, which every later grade 5 rehearsal uses. Five sub-skills, two groups and 10 sessions. It runs beside ELA grade 5 unit 1 and health grade 5 unit 15 (weeks 1 to 4) (Cross-subject). Sessions 1 to 10 of the year, weeks 1 to 5.
