LEARNING: Two groups. The four-week goal and the three-week practice record start on session 1 (the carry-out cues) and are judged before the Check session. Group 1, goals and plans: a four-week goal on the goal steps card, tracked weekly, with what to drop decided when two goals compete for time (SM4); a multi-week class project planned backward from a deadline and recovered when a step slips, with what the slip cost (SM5); keeping on task through the long project when friends offer something more fun and when the next step gets hard, using the focus plan and its try-again step (try another way, then ask), and what giving in would cost (SM3; it also teaches AASL.V.D.1, trying again when a task gets hard, placed in SEL by library). Group 2, purpose and setbacks: a stretch goal for a character facing a setback that costs something (a free afternoon), with two steps, a helper and a backup plan (SA7); when a friend in a story says "you're just not good at it", the practice record used to explain the setback as a sign to change strategy or get help, never belief alone (SA8; it also teaches AASL.V.D.2, skill grows with practice and help, placed in SEL by library); a purpose found for an interest that costs practice time, decided privately (SA9). Retrieval: the grade 4 rows (units 8 and 12) in the openings; health grade 5 unit 15's four-week log (weeks 1 to 4) opens SM4 as retrieval where the school runs health. End-of-unit evidence: an unseen page (a backup plan for a character's setback; a setback explained from an invented record; which goal to drop and why) and the focus plan's try-again step rehearsed from an unseen card. The course never records a student's own answer to SA7 or SA9. Carry it out: the weekly goal check. Family activity: plan one family job backward from its deadline. Tools: the goal steps card, the backward planner, the practice record, the focus plan card, the private log. Curio Class writes the planner, the records and cases and the page. Provisional cost for 30: about $10 printing.
WHY: After unit 13 because steady feelings come before long goals; its five weeks hold the four-week goal (the progression's pace note). Six sub-skills in two groups of three, each with two Fluency sessions, so 10 sessions. Health grade 5 unit 15 (weeks 1 to 4) starts its goal log first; ELA grade 5 unit 2 (course days 42 to 80) runs its research beside it (Cross-subject). Sessions 11 to 20 of the year, weeks 6 to 10.
