LEARNING: Three groups. Group 1, a friend's side: an invented friend whose family is moving across town mid-year, the friend's view taken with the shoes switch and how one's own view would change in that place (SO1); mixed clues from an invented friend who says they are fine but is pulling away, a check-in, the answer respected, and a trusted adult named to tell if the worry stays (SO4); the care steps acted with a partner for an invented friend whose best friend has moved away, even when it costs time with others, and a follow-up planned (SO3). Group 2, talking it through: the full talk turn card in an invented hard conversation about a friendship changing (a friend joins a new group), where saying back costs patience (RS1); a disagreement where any fair solution costs each side something, worked with a partner using the I-statement, and a compromise both can keep (RS5); two invented cases, a friend who will be in a different class next year and a friend who will only play if the student leaves another child out, planned with the I-statement, keeping the first friendship and stepping back from the second with a trusted adult's help, the opening of each talk rehearsed with a partner (RS2). Group 3, help and hold: two problems sized on the meter, then asking a teacher for help when friends are watching rehearsed with a partner playing the teacher, and help offered to an invented new classmate (RS8); the refusal steps against a card character who adds a social cost ("then you're not in our group"), the no held and another friend named to turn to (RS6). Retrieval: the grade 4 rows (units 7, 10 and 11) in the openings; health grade 5 unit 17's refusal steps (weeks 10 to 14) open RS6 as retrieval where the school runs health. End-of-unit evidence: an unseen scene page (mixed clues and a check-in; a compromise where both give something; a friendship to step back from and who helps) and the refusal steps rehearsed with the card playing the social cost. Carry it out: "say back first" in hard class talks. Family activity: plan how to keep in touch with someone far away, real or made up. Tools: the shoes switch card, the talk turn card, the I-statement frame, the problem size meter, the refusal card, scene cards. Curio Class writes the cases and page. Provisional cost for 30: about $10 printing.
WHY: After unit 15 because holding a no against a social cost follows checking against a crowd. Eight sub-skills, three groups and 11 sessions. Health grade 5 unit 18 (conflict steps and care, weeks 17 to 19) runs in the same weeks, and unit 17 (refusal, weeks 10 to 14) came before (Cross-subject). Sessions 31 to 41 of the year, weeks 16 to 21.
